  "live_records": {
    "q-350960": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350960",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{5} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{5}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{3})^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{18}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{18}-(\\frac{{e}^{18}}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(18{e}^{18}-{e}^{18}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
