    "q-49712": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49712",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{log}_{4}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}{\\int }_{1}^{e}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[uv{|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(x){|}_{1}^{e}-{\\int }_{1}^{e}x(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}[e-x{|}_{1}^{e}\\,] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}(e-e+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
